---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import { getAllTools, getCategories } from '../lib/supabase';

const tools = await getAllTools();
const categories = await getCategories();
const featuredTools = tools.slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title="AI Tools HQ | Compare 500+ AI Tools Free (2026 Reviews)"
  description="Find the best AI tool in 60 seconds. 500+ tools with ratings, pricing & honest reviews. Compare ChatGPT vs Claude, Midjourney vs DALL-E & more."
>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Find the Perfect AI Tool</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Expert reviews of 500+ AI tools to boost your productivity</p>

      <div class="search-box">
        <input type="search" placeholder="Search AI tools..." id="search" />
      </div>

      <div class="categories">
        {categories.map(cat => (
          <a href={`/category/${cat.toLowerCase()}`} class="category-pill">
            {cat}
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Featured Tools -->
    <section class="featured">
      <h2>Featured AI Tools</h2>
      <div class="tools-grid">
        {featuredTools.map(tool => (
          <ToolCard tool={tool} />
        ))}
      </div>
      <a href="/tools" class="view-all">View All Tools →</a>
    </section>

    <!-- Categories Section -->
    <section class="category-section">
      <h2>Browse by Category</h2>
      <div class="category-grid">
        {categories.map(cat => (
          <a href={`/category/${cat.toLowerCase()}`} class="category-card">
            <h3>{cat}</h3>
            <p>{tools.filter(t => t.category === cat).length} tools</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Popular Comparisons -->
    <section class="comparisons">
      <h2>Popular Comparisons</h2>
      <div class="comparison-links">
        <a href="/compare/jasper-vs-copy-ai">Jasper vs Copy.ai</a>
        <a href="/compare/midjourney-vs-dall-e">Midjourney vs DALL-E</a>
        <a href="/compare/chatgpt-vs-claude">ChatGPT vs Claude</a>
        <a href="/best/ai-writing-tools">Best AI Writing Tools 2026</a>
        <a href="/best/free-ai-image-generators">Free AI Image Generators</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SEO Content Section -->
    <section class="seo-content">
      <h2>Your Complete Guide to AI Tools in 2026</h2>
      
      <div class="seo-grid">
        <div class="seo-block">
          <h3>Why Use AI Tools?</h3>
          <p>AI tools have revolutionized how we work, create, and solve problems. From generating marketing copy in seconds to creating stunning images from text descriptions, artificial intelligence is no longer a futuristic concept—it's an essential part of the modern toolkit. Whether you're a solo entrepreneur, creative professional, or enterprise team, the right AI tools can multiply your output while freeing you to focus on strategy and creativity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="seo-block">
          <h3>How We Review AI Tools</h3>
          <p>Every tool in our directory undergoes hands-on testing by our team. We evaluate ease of use, output quality, pricing transparency, and real-world applications. We don't just list features—we tell you what actually works, what's overhyped, and where each tool fits in your workflow. Our reviews are updated regularly as tools release new features and competitors emerge.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="seo-block">
          <h3>Finding the Right AI Tool</h3>
          <p>With hundreds of AI tools available, finding the right one can feel overwhelming. Start by identifying your specific need: Are you writing blog posts? Creating social media graphics? Automating code reviews? Then compare tools within that category using our detailed reviews and side-by-side comparisons. Consider factors like pricing, learning curve, integration options, and whether free tiers meet your needs.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="seo-block">
          <h3>AI Tools by Use Case</h3>
          <p>Looking for <a href="/category/writing">AI writing assistants</a>? Tools like Jasper and Copy.ai excel at marketing copy. Need <a href="/category/image">AI image generators</a>? Midjourney and DALL-E lead the pack. For developers, <a href="/category/coding">AI coding assistants</a> like GitHub Copilot and Cursor are game-changers. Browse our categories to discover tools tailored to your workflow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="seo-faq">
        <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        
        <details>
          <summary>What are AI tools?</summary>
          <p>AI tools are software applications powered by artificial intelligence that can perform tasks traditionally requiring human intelligence. This includes writing content, generating images, analyzing data, coding, and much more. Modern AI tools use large language models (LLMs) and machine learning to understand context and produce human-quality output.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Are AI tools free to use?</summary>
          <p>Many AI tools offer free tiers or trials that let you test their capabilities. Tools like ChatGPT, Canva's AI features, and several image generators have generous free plans. However, professional-grade output and higher usage limits typically require paid subscriptions ranging from $10-100/month.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Which AI tool is best for beginners?</summary>
          <p>For beginners, we recommend starting with ChatGPT for general AI assistance, Canva for AI-powered design, and Grammarly for writing improvement. These tools have intuitive interfaces, helpful tutorials, and free tiers that make it easy to learn AI without a steep learning curve.</p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can AI tools replace human workers?</summary>
          <p>AI tools are best used to augment human capabilities, not replace them. They excel at repetitive tasks, first drafts, and data processing, but still require human oversight for quality, creativity, and strategic decisions. The most successful users combine AI efficiency with human judgment.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 2rem;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 0 0 2rem 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    opacity: 0.9;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .search-box input {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 500px;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 50px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
  }

  .categories {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .category-pill {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
    color: white;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .category-pill:hover {
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.3);
  }

  .featured, .category-section, .comparisons {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 4rem auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .tools-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(350px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .view-all {
    display: block;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: #667eea;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .category-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .category-card {
    background: #f8f9fa;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: transform 0.2s, box-shadow 0.2s;
  }

  .category-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
  }

  .category-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .category-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .comparison-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .comparison-links a {
    background: #e9ecef;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: #333;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  .comparison-links a:hover {
    background: #dee2e6;
  }

  .seo-content {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 4rem auto;
    padding: 3rem 2rem;
    background: #f8f9fa;
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .seo-content h2 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .seo-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .seo-block {
    background: white;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
  }

  .seo-block h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .seo-block p {
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .seo-block a {
    color: #667eea;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .seo-block a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .seo-faq {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .seo-faq h3 {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .seo-faq details {
    background: white;
    border-radius: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .seo-faq summary {
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #333;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .seo-faq summary::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #667eea;
  }

  .seo-faq details[open] summary::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .seo-faq details p {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1rem;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>

<script>
  const search = document.getElementById('search');
  search?.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    const query = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).value.toLowerCase();
    if (query.length >= 2) {
      window.location.href = `/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`;
    }
  });
</script>
